quran[21]{c,v,t}:
  26,40,Perhaps we may follow the magicians if they are the victors!’
  26,41,"So when the magicians came, they said to Pharaoh: ‘Shall we indeed receive a reward if we are the victors?’"
  26,42,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Of course! Then indeed you shall be among those near (to me, by entering my inner court).’"
  26,43,Musa (Moses) said to them (the magicians): ‘Throw down what you are going to throw.’
  26,44,"So they threw down their ropes and sticks and said: ‘By the might of Pharaoh, we shall surely be the victors.’"
  26,45,"Then, Musa (Moses) threw down his staff; behold, it was swallowing up what they had faked."
  26,46,"Then, the magicians were made to fall, prostrating."
  26,47,"They said: ‘We believe in the Lord of worlds,"
  26,48,the Lord of Musa (Moses) and Harun (Aaron).’
  26,49,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Do you believe in Him before I permit you? He (Moses) is indeed your chief who has taught you magic. So you shall soon know (about your end). I will surely cut off your hands and your feet from opposite sides, and I will surely crucify you all.’"
  26,50,"They said: ‘No harm (in it). Indeed, we are to return to our Lord."
  26,51,"Indeed, we hope our Lord will forgive us our sins for being the first of the believers.’"
  26,52,"Then We revealed to Musa (Moses), (saying:) ‘Leave with My servants by night, for you shall indeed be pursued.’"
  26,53,Then Pharaoh sent heralds to the cities.
  26,54,(Announcing:) ‘These (Israelites) are indeed a small gang.
  26,55,"And indeed, they are enraging us."
  26,56,"And indeed, all of us are alert.’"
  26,57,"So We expelled them (i.e. Pharaoh and his people) from gardens and springs,"
  26,58,and (from) treasures and noble dwellings.
  26,59,"Thus it is, and We made the Children of Israel inherit them."
  26,60,Then they pursued them at sunrise.
